<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet>
    <title>Quiz 8 - MTH 305 - Regan</title>

    <p>
        This quiz covers Markov chains, and retakes on single and multiple
        equation ODE models, their fixed point(s), and stability.
        Read all <term>DIRECTIONS</term> carefully.
        Good luck!
    </p>

    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                In the Coimbatore forest, Tamil Nadu, India, elephants migrate
                between three areas, Anaikatti (A), Periya Thadagam (PT), and
                Nanjundapuram (N).
                The probability that an elephant will migrate from one region to
                another on any given day can be summarized as follows:
                <ul>
                    <li>10% chance of moving from PT to A</li>
                    <li>15% chance of moving from PT to N</li>
                    <li>9% chance of moving from A to PT</li>
                    <li>22% chance of moving from A to N</li>
                    <li>8% chance of moving from N to A</li>
                    <li>26% chance of moving from N to PT</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Create the appropriate probability transition matrix M.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Is there a steady-state vector?
                    Explain your reasoning.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Let's say you are given the following output from Python:
                </p>

                <image source="images/8quiz_markov.png" width="60%">
                    <shortdescription>
                        Eigenvalue and eigenvector output for a probability
                        transition matrix.
                    </shortdescription>
                </image>

                <p>
                    What is the steady-state vector?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What percentage of the elephants will be in each area in the
                    long run?
                    Does this depend on how many elephants start in each region?
                    Explain.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>

    <p>
        <term>Retake of 2D ODE Models: </term>
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="2in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find the fixed point(s) for the following system of differential
                equations.
                <md>
                    <mrow>
                    \frac{dx}{dt} \amp = x - x^2 - xy \\
                    </mrow>
                    <mrow>
                    \frac{dy}{dt} \amp = 3y - xy - 2y^2 \\
                     </mrow>
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                Determine the stability of one of the fixed points.
                Note: just need to state whether it is stable/unstable if you
                don't know specifics (e.g., spiral sink).
                Show all work.
            </p>

            <p>
                Remember, the stability is based on the eigenvalues of the
                Jacobian matrix
                <md>
                    \textrm{Jacobian,}\,\, J = \begin{bmatrix}\frac{\partial f}{\partial{x}} &amp; \frac{\partial f}{\partial{y}} \\  \\ \frac{\partial g}{\partial{x}} &amp; \frac{\partial g}{\partial{y}}\end{bmatrix},
                </md>
                where the trace, <m>T</m>, and determinant, <m>D</m>, give the
                eigenvalues of
                <md>
                    \lambda_{1}, \lambda_{2} = \frac{T \pm \sqrt{T^{2} - 4D}}{2}.
                </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <p>
        <term>Last Retake of 1D ODE Models: </term>
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Determine fixed point(s) and corresponding stability for the
                following differential equation.
                Show all work.
                <md>
                    \frac{dx}{dt} = \cos(x)
                </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>